Strip the output of a `cc_common.link` link at the `-Cstrip` level of rustc.

Under `experimental_use_cc_common_link`, rustc links only with `native_libs_recorder`. So `-Cstrip` strips a copy of
the object that the build discards, and the output of `cc_common.link` keeps its debug info and its symbols. This
applies to the `strip_level` of the toolchain and to a `-Cstrip` in the flags of a target.

`cc_common.link` strips only for `--strip`, which applies to every cc link. So take the last `-Cstrip` level that
rustc gets, and set the `strip_debug_symbols` variable for that link. The cc toolchain then strips the debug info as
its linker needs: `-Wl,-S`, or `/DEBUG:NONE` for an MSVC link. On macOS, the `@llvm` toolchain strips after it writes
the dSYM. For `symbols`, also pass the flag that rustc uses: `-Wl,-x` on Apple, `-Wl,--strip-all` on the others. An
MSVC link keeps the symbols in the PDB, so it needs no other flag, and a stripped MSVC link declares no PDB.
